  "format": "op offset: the server offset from samples (server − local milliseconds, recorded oldest first) = expect: of the last 20 samples, sorted ascending, the one at index (count − 1) / 2 rounded down (the lower middle for an even count); null with no sample. op mint: a clock for deviceID holding samples and its last issued stamp (lastMilliseconds, lastCounter; lastMilliseconds −1 before the first) mints the stamp of a change made at local time eventTime, to a field whose replica stamp is seen (or null), at local time now = expect (null when there is no offset yet), and expectLast is the clock's state afterwards (its last issued stamp and earlierCounters). earlierCounters (milliseconds as a decimal string → the last counter issued in that millisecond) are the counters the clock remembers below lastMilliseconds: only keys below lastMilliseconds and not negative, at most the 64 latest (the smallest go first), both as given and after a mint. milliseconds = max(eventTime + offset, min(seen's milliseconds, now + offset + 86400000) + 1), at least 0 and at most 9999999999999; counter = lastCounter + 1 when the milliseconds equal lastMilliseconds, else earlierCounters[milliseconds] + 1 when remembered, else 0; past 9999 the next millisecond, whose counter follows the same rule. Afterwards: milliseconds above lastMilliseconds make them the last stamp (the previous last stamp's counter, when there was one, joins earlierCounters); equal ones move lastCounter; lower ones are remembered in earlierCounters.",
  "status": "Written with WP2; built by scripts/schema/build-vectors.mjs from its reference clock.",
